newFindings.evidence:
AC-1.3/TC-1.3a requires fenced code to remain unchanged through inference smoothing. `smoothPromptHandler` computes `cleaned = cleanPrompt(text)` and sends that value to `provider.smoothPrompt` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:83`, `packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:104`). `cleanPrompt` applies whitespace and casing replacements to the whole prompt (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/smoothing.ts:3`-`10`). Direct repro: `cleanPrompt("fix this
```ts
const  i = 1;

	return  i;
```
thanks")` returned `"fix this
```ts
const I = 1;

return I;
```
thanks"`, changing spaces, tab indentation, and `i` inside the fenced block. The existing fenced test uses `const value = 1;` and a provider stub that returns a fixed preserved block (`packages/lhc/test/smoothing-recovery.test.ts:168`-`193`), so it does not prove byte-identical preservation for fenced content affected by deterministic cleaning.

